  },
  "design": {
   "extraction_status": "extracted",
   "value": "A within-subject block-design fMRI study in which 32 treatment-seeking, nicotine-dependent smokers viewed smoking-related and neutral images during two back-to-back presentations: first while instructed to allow themselves to crave and then while instructed to resist the urge to smoke. The study examined smoking-related cue versus neutral cue contrasts and comparisons between craving, resisting, and resistance strategies.",
